Changes made in srobroek/harness-plugins, 2026-11:

- Renamed the skill to business-rules-cel-authoring.
- Replaced the "Locate or Create Environment" step. The skill now reads the project's generated environment,
  descriptor set and profile manifest, and stops when none covers the scope. It never writes an envConfig.
- Removed the protoc descriptor-set alias, -proto_db, and the advice on protoTypes, imports and enum variables.
- Replaced "go install ...@latest" with an install from a verified release.
- Removed the advice to prefer namespaced variables of simple types over a map; scopes are message-typed.
- Restricted the policy section to the supported policy profile: one flat match block, a condition on every
  choice but the final one, an unconditional final choice, no variables, aggregate, nested rule, explanation or
  imports, and outputs of the slot type. Noted that the v0.4.0 release has no -format=policy.
- Added the steps that run the project's reference checker and add the cases to the project's suite.
- Removed skippedTestCases, which the v0.4.0 release does not have.
- Left out the upstream examples and references, which hand-write environments.
